diff --git a/docs/spec/m17.md b/docs/spec/m17.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5891424
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/spec/m17.md
@@ -0,0 +1,132 @@
+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later -->
+<!-- Copyright (c) 2026 lyra XE1POC -->
+
+# M17
+
+M17 stream mode voice on a channel: `core/m17` (frames, engine, voice), `core/radio/radio_m17.c` (the radio core's
+side) and Codec 2 at 3200 bit/s (`core/codec2`, vendored, LGPL-2.1). Built with `CONFIG_M17` (off by default,
+[build-config.md](../build-config.md)); it runs on the air interface ([air-interface.md](air-interface.md)) of an
+air-framed mode, so it needs `P25`, `NXDN` or `YSF` too.
+
+Source: the M17 Protocol Specification (spec.m17project.org; the document is GFDL-1.3). Nothing here comes from
+another implementation. Section names in the code's comments are the specification's chapter names.
+
+State: host tested only. No M17 transmission has been received from or sent to another M17 radio, hotspot or
+modem (section 8).
+
+## 1. What is written
+
+| Part | State |
+|---|---|
+| Stream mode voice, 3200 bit/s Codec 2, no encryption | receive and transmit |
+| LSF, LICH late entry (the LSF rebuilt from six chunks) | receive and transmit |
+| CAN squelch, digital monitor (every CAN) | receive |
+| META field | sent as zeros, not read |
+| Packet mode, BERT, 1600 bit/s voice + data, encryption, signed streams | not written: such a call is heard (the view shows it) and stays silent |
+
+## 2. Physical layer
+
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Profile | 4800 symbols/s, 4 levels, RRC alpha 0.5, outer deviation 2400 Hz, continuous, 12.5 kHz (`m17_air_mode`) |
+| Dibits | +3 `01`, +1 `00`, -1 `10`, -3 `11`: the air interface's map, MSB first |
+| Preamble | 192 symbols of +3 -3 (byte 0x77), the last one -3, opposite the LSF sync's first |
+| Frame | 192 symbols, 40 ms: an 8-symbol sync burst and 368 payload bits |
+| Sync bursts | LSF 0x55F7, stream 0xFF5D, EoT 0x555D (192 symbols of it end a transmission); packet 0x75FF and BERT 0xDF55 are not listed |
+| Idle | the preamble byte |
+
+The profile's patterns: the stream sync (8 symbols, 1 error), the preamble's last 8 symbols with the LSF sync (16
+symbols, 2 errors, start only) and the EoT (8 symbols, 1 error). The stream and EoT patterns carry
+`AIR_SYNC_PERIODIC`: an 8-symbol pattern of outer symbols only turns up in the payload, and the soft modem retimed on
+those imitations until it was told to take the pattern, while locked, only a frame (or two) after the last sync
+([air-interface.md](air-interface.md) 6).
+
+The HR_C7000 provider transmits through the chip's own pulse filter (DMR's root raised cosine 0.2,
+[modem-hrc7000.md](modem-hrc7000.md) 10.3), so the fit says `AIR_FIT_SHAPE_APPROX`: the transmitted spectrum is wider
+than M17's alpha 0.5 and its eye at an M17 receiver's RRC 0.5 filter is not the specification's. The deviation (2400
+Hz) is NXDN96's and is in the chip's range. Receive goes through the soft modem on the discriminator tap, which
+takes either pulse (m17Test models both).
+
+## 3. Frames and FEC
+
+| Item | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| LSF | DST 6, SRC 6, TYPE 2, META 14 bytes, CRC 2: 240 bits, 4 flush bits, K=5 rate 1/2 code (G1 = 1 + D^3 + D^4, G2 = 1 + D + D^2 + D^4; `core/fec/conv.c`, the same code as NXDN's), 488 bits punctured by P1 (a 1, then 1011 fifteen times; 61 entries used 8 times) to 368 |
+| Stream frame | LICH (48 bits) in four Golay (24,12) words, 96 bits (`core/fec/golay.c`: the same code, g = 0xC75, as TIA-102's); FN 16 bits and 128 bits of stream data, 4 flush bits, coded to 296 bits, every 12th dropped (P2), 272 bits; the two concatenated |
+| LICH | 40 bits of the LSF (chunk LICH_CNT, 0-5) and LICH_CNT in the top 3 bits of byte 5 |
+| FN | from 0, +1 a frame, 15 bits; bit 15 set on the last frame |
+| Interleaver | Type 3 bit x to Type 4 bit (45x + 92x^2) mod 368 |
+| Randomizer | payload bit k XOR bit 7 - k % 8 of byte (k / 8) % 46 of the specification's sequence |
+| CRC | polynomial 0x5935, initial 0xFFFF, MSB first, no final XOR; over the 30 LSF bytes it gives 0 |
+| TYPE | bit 0 stream, bits 1-2 data type (2 voice), 3-4 encryption, 5-6 subtype, 7-10 CAN, 11 signed |
+| Address | base-40, the first character least significant (`m17_addr_encode`); 0xFFFFFFFFFFFF broadcast, shown and stored as `ALL` |
+
+Receive decodes with soft values where the provider gives them: the sign bit of a dibit from the symbol's sign, the
+other from its distance to the inner level; punctured bits enter the Viterbi decoder as 0.
+
+## 4. Receive
+
+The head hook (`m17_engine.c`) sees each whole frame (the interleaver spreads the LICH over it):
+
+| Frame | Taken when |
+|---|---|
+| EoT | never: the call ends |
+| LSF | its CRC holds |
+| Stream | its LICH decodes (four Golay words, LICH_CNT 0-5), or inside a call when the Viterbi decoder corrected 15 bits or fewer (frames of noise: 27 or more, m17Test) |
+| Without a sync, inside a call | as a stream frame, up to three in a row |
+
+A call starts with an LSF frame, or with a stream frame (late entry): then the LSF is rebuilt from the six LICH
+chunks and checked by its CRC. It is played when it is stream mode, data type voice, not encrypted, and its CAN is the
+channel's (any CAN with digital monitor). A frame with FN bit 15, an EoT, or three frames without a sync end it.
+
+## 5. Codeplug
+
+Kind 7 ([channel-modes.md](channel-modes.md) 4). Tag: no system, flag bit 0 transmit allowed. The base record is
+the safe stand-in (DMR, receive only) as for the other modes.
+
+| Offset | Size | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 1 | Bits 0-3 CAN (0-15), bits 4-7 0 (kept by the editor) |
+| 1 | 9 | Destination, ASCII, space padded; all spaces reads as `ALL` (broadcast) |
+
+A zeroed or missing block is CAN 0, destination `ALL`. Radio-wide record (key 0x0A00 + 7): the source call sign, 9
+ASCII characters; blank, the radio's name (the CPS call sign) is sent. Call signs are upper-cased; a character
+outside the M17 alphabet is sent as a space (the Codeplug Editor warns).
+
+The VFO and a channel made M17 for now use the RAM settings (CAN 0, destination `ALL`). The radio's channel editor
+has M17 on the Mode row, with CAN and Destination rows; a save writes the tag as YSF's does
+([ysf-codeplug.md](ysf-codeplug.md) 2.4). The Quick menu's Code and Dest tiles do not change M17's CAN or destination
+yet.
+
+## 6. Radio core and voice
+
+`radio_m17.c` fills the air modes' `radio_air_ops_t` (PTT, time-out and release as for P25, NXDN and YSF) and
+`radio_view_t.m17` (the call heard, what PTT calls, the CAN sent). The home screen shows the destination on the talk
+line and `CAN n` on the chips line.
+
+Voice (`m17_voice.c`, the shape of `p25Voice.c`): one 8-byte Codec 2 frame per 20 ms audio block, two per stream
+frame; playback starts with four frames queued. With no encoder frame ready the engine sends Codec 2 silence
+(`M17_C2_SILENCE`: all-zero bits are not silence in this mode, they decode at speech level).
+
+| Resource | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Codec 2 state and FFT tables | 30,752 B on a 64-bit host, in a 31,744 B static arena (`M17_VOICE_ARENA`); allocated once, by the audio task's first block |
+| Stack | about 20 KB measured on a host for encode or decode (512-point FFT buffers on the stack). The HR_C7000 platform's audio task stack is 5632 words with `CONFIG_M17` (1536 without) and the FreeRTOS heap 56 KB (40 KB) |
+| CPU | host x86-64 with an FPU: about 180 us to encode and 14 us to decode a 20 ms block (m17VoiceTest). The CK803S has no FPU: Codec 2 runs as software floating point there. Not measured; encoding in real time is doubtful |
+
+## 7. Tests
+
+| Test | Covers |
+|---|---|
+| `tests/host/m17Test.c` | the specification's CRC vectors and address example; LSF and stream frames through the FEC with symbol errors, hard and soft; LICH late entry; EoT; noise; two engines on made-up providers (a call, late entry, CAN squelch, digital monitor, a slow encoder, an abort); a call through the soft modem at RRC 0.5 and 0.2 with noise |
+| `tests/host/m17VoiceTest.c` | Codec 2 in its arena; synthetic voice encoded to stream frames and decoded at about the same level; the silence frames |
+| `tests/host/radioCoreTest.c` (`radioCoreTestM17`) | a stored M17 channel through the radio core: PTT heard by a far engine with the channel's fields, the far radio heard, another CAN silent |
+| `site/tests/modes.test.mjs` | the editor's kind 7 module |
+
+## 8. Not verified
+
+- On air: interoperability with any other M17 equipment (radios, MMDVM hotspots, M17 modems). Only this firmware's
+  own frames have been decoded, by this firmware's own decoder, on the host.
+- The transmit pulse (RRC 0.2 instead of 0.5, section 2) at another M17 receiver.
+- Codec 2 real time, its stack and RAM on the radio: no cross build was run.
+- Codec 2 voice quality on the radio's microphone and speaker paths (the microphone level into the encoder).
